  "text": "The Tortoise and the Hare There was once a tortoise that slowly crawled through a forest. Bling bling A bouncing hare saw the tortoise and made fun of him. Make way, make way, I'm bouncing through. Hey, Slowpoke, didn't you hear me? Move out of the way. The angered tortoise stopped walking and said, Hey, let's race to the top of the mountain and see who gets there faster. You think you can beat me? Fine, let's do it. Ready, set, go! So Hare bounced away and Tortoise slowly crawled. Boing, boing, and away went Hare. While slow poke Tortoise crept and crawled With bullets of sweat dripping down. Now where is Tortoise? Wow, he is so far behind. It'll take him forever to catch up. So I think I'll take a nap. While Hare slept, Tortoise never stopped walking. Blump, blump. Sure enough, Tortoise crawled past sleepyhead Hare, and he crawled to the top of the hill. Hey, hare. I beat you. What? What's going on? Hare woke up and scurried up the hill. But it was too late. Tortoise was already resting under a tree at the top of the mountain. No, this can't be. I lost a slowpoke tortoise.",
